d that came with it it was actually  cracked so i had to call it microsoft  and they gave me  a link to download the software and the  drivers for so let me get the cd hold on  i couldn't find the cd but you know that  shows you how much i need it i i don't  you can download it anyway if you want  to you don't have to use a cd because  there might be a more modern there might  be an updated version of your firmware  or software for you to use with your  mouse so  if you get a new mouse or you get some  new hardware i recommend you download  the drivers from the manufacturer's  website  and the reason i knew that it was a  microsoft wireless laser mouse 6000  version 2.0 was obviously it was on the  box but it also says it it'll say on the  bottom of the mouse what version you  have and everything  so um  yeah that's it  um so go ahead and enjoy the uh software  part of this  here's the software part of this review  in order to access the customization  software for the particular buttons i  showed you on the mouse  using windows vista's innovative start  menu search feature type in mouse and  hit enter which will select the first  program microsoft mouse  this will bring up your window with  mouse properties  um looks just like microsoft built it in  it's got all these hardware and software  tabs  uh the first thing you can do is program  what the different buttons do if i if i  hover over the left button as you can  see there it is click here so there is  11 the right button wheel  rear thumb and front thumb and that's  exactly where my thumb sits in that  little little  curve right there this is the actual  connected device which i'm using to as  i'm recording this video if i go to the  buttons tab  it's it shows that we're right-handed  which means that the left button is the  primary button  uh double click speed which which  basically dictates how fast you have to  click to open a folder  um so that's how  that's how you can test your  settings  under pointers 